    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-15T21:16:55+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-15T21:16:55+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T11:46:55Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T11:46:55Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of the state slowly drifts to the southeast and is forecast to be located in the Tasman Sea on Monday, while extending a ridge over much of South Australia through to Tuesday. A trough of low pressure over Queensland pushes into the far northeast of SA until Monday, as another trough moves into far southwestern parts later on Tuesday and moves southeast across the state into Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-15T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of light showers about the Gammon Ranges, slight chance elsewhere. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 21.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:10am to 2:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 25.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers south of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. High chance of showers south of Yunta, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then becoming northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
